Does Shelly know about this?

00:29:02.770 --> 00:29:03.730
What does she think?

00:29:05.150 --> 00:29:06.750
Shelly's a trusting person, Maurice.

00:29:07.940 --> 00:29:09.400
She takes things at face value.

00:29:11.370 --> 00:29:13.710
She doesn't suspect ulterior motives in people.

00:29:15.770 --> 00:29:16.770
Ulterior motives?

00:29:18.810 --> 00:29:21.470
Holling, I'm just trying to do what's right by Uncle Elvie.

00:29:23.110 --> 00:29:26.490
Maurice, we both know that this has nothing to do with Uncle Elvie.

00:29:28.520 --> 00:29:29.980
No, you've got to sleep, Lou.

00:29:30.500 --> 00:29:33.640
Have you given any thought to Miranda?

00:29:35.020 --> 00:29:36.940
Do you know what you're depriving your daughter of?

00:29:37.890 --> 00:29:41.060
Well, you got one thing right. She's my daughter.

00:29:42.620 --> 00:29:44.360
Just what the hell is that supposed to mean?

00:29:46.680 --> 00:29:47.740
Maurice, you're my friend.

00:29:49.140 --> 00:29:51.140
I'm sorry if you felt grief over losing Shelly,

00:29:51.220 --> 00:29:55.350
but she's my wife, and Randy's our child.

00:30:00.060 --> 00:30:04.810
I hope she's got her mother's sense, because her father's a damn fool.

00:30:17.440 --> 00:30:19.080
Would you hand me the pushpins, please?

00:30:19.380 --> 00:30:19.900
Yeah, sure.

00:30:22.210 --> 00:30:22.610
Thank you.

00:30:24.610 --> 00:30:26.470
Maybe you better get inside and get warm.

00:30:26.510 --> 00:30:27.410
I can finish this.

00:30:27.840 --> 00:30:28.980
No, I'm fine, really.

00:30:29.140 --> 00:30:29.960
I think I just need to...

00:30:31.140 --> 00:30:34.660
You know, when your feet are cold, you'll be cold.

00:30:35.740 --> 00:30:37.080
Actually, my feet are fine.

00:30:37.260 --> 00:30:38.620
In those thin little boots.

00:30:39.700 --> 00:30:42.550
Well, they were cold, but I guess they got used to it.

00:30:42.610 --> 00:30:43.730
I can hardly feel them at all now.

00:30:45.840 --> 00:30:47.080
I think we should go see Phil.

00:30:47.680 --> 00:30:50.480
A doctor ought to look at your feet.

00:30:51.270 --> 00:30:52.010
A doctor? Why?

00:30:52.690 --> 00:30:55.390
Well, from what you've just said, I think you have frostbite.

00:30:56.990 --> 00:30:58.050
Frostbite? Really?

00:30:58.720 --> 00:30:59.980
We probably caught it in town.

00:31:00.500 --> 00:31:01.320
Let me help you.

00:31:02.990 --> 00:31:05.520
You want to walk very, very carefully.

00:31:05.860 --> 00:31:06.200
Okay.

00:31:06.600 --> 00:31:08.300
We don't want to do any damage.

00:31:09.890 --> 00:31:12.060
You okay?

00:31:12.540 --> 00:31:12.700
Yeah.

00:31:14.390 --> 00:31:15.630
Let me see.

00:31:19.360 --> 00:31:19.820
Does it hurt?

00:31:20.260 --> 00:31:23.670
There's no sign of gangrene.

00:31:24.090 --> 00:31:24.390
Gangrene?

00:31:24.510 --> 00:31:26.310
I said there's no sign of gangrene.

00:31:27.960 --> 00:31:29.320
I'm gonna put you on some ampicillin

00:31:29.320 --> 00:31:29.980
and keep you off your...

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:40.030
feet for a while. You should feel better. Let me have the other one. I feel so stupid. This is all my

00:31:40.030 --> 00:31:46.280
fault. Why? You weren't the one trying to tame the Yukon and clear your ankle boots. I brought

00:31:46.280 --> 00:31:54.390
you here to this arctic wasteland, this frozen jungle. No, honey, we came together. I wanted to

00:31:54.390 --> 00:31:59.970
come just as much as you did. We've ruined our lives, Michelle. Idaho is as far north

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:00.840
as we should have gone.

00:32:01.280 --> 00:32:03.280
Now we're trapped here, and there's no escape.

00:32:03.500 --> 00:32:03.900
Phil.

00:32:04.200 --> 00:32:05.420
It's not just a contract.

00:32:05.840 --> 00:32:07.300
We'll just never get out from under.

00:32:08.092 --> 00:32:11.252
Every cent we had is socked away into a piece of land that...

00:32:11.388 --> 00:32:15.868
paralyzes me with terror so we'll sell the land nobody wants to buy the land

00:32:17.180 --> 00:32:18.800
It's an albatross around our necks.

00:32:20.572 --> 00:32:23.852
No, we have gone down the rabbit hole, Michelle, and look where we ended up.

00:32:24.032 --> 00:32:26.932
In a place where moose copulate with cars.

00:32:27.804 --> 00:32:29.984
A place where people just drop the U.S. mail.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:30.860
out of airplanes.

00:32:31.980 --> 00:32:34.640
A place where log tossing is considered high culture.

00:32:36.140 --> 00:32:38.680
We have gone down the rabbit hole.

00:32:40.620 --> 00:32:41.580
There's no way out.

00:32:58.444 --> 00:32:59.744
I'm closed, Maurice.

00:33:00.120 --> 00:33:02.360
I just came in to get this bonnet. What do you think?

00:33:04.610 --> 00:33:05.870
It's for Founders Day.

00:33:06.150 --> 00:33:08.910
I really like the cutaway and derby you wore last year.

00:33:09.750 --> 00:33:13.110
Don't you have any English toffees?

00:33:14.040 --> 00:33:14.580
Good Lord.

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:17.730
right under your nose.

00:33:18.700 --> 00:33:28.320
See the light still on above the brick.

00:33:31.020 --> 00:33:31.760
I guess there.

00:33:32.108 --> 00:33:34.128
He's putting Miranda to bed right now.

00:33:35.756 --> 00:33:36.736
Holling and Shelley.

00:33:38.412 --> 00:33:40.412
bending over

00:33:40.812 --> 00:33:41.652
Tucking her in.

00:33:42.636 --> 00:33:44.576
Is this about that Uncle Elvie business?

00:33:45.164 --> 00:33:46.084
You know about that?

00:33:46.348 --> 00:33:47.548
She only mentioned it.

00:33:48.844 --> 00:33:51.744
I swear, Maurice, what Holly puts up with from you.

00:33:52.108 --> 00:33:52.668
Harling.

00:33:53.260 --> 00:33:57.620
Well, I'm the injured party here, throwing my gifts back in my face like that.

00:33:58.284 --> 00:33:59.984
You're lucky you didn't knock your block.

00:34:00.860 --> 00:34:05.620
The way you've been trying to make him out to be some kind of a metaphysical cuckold.

00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:07.840
Now, you hold on just a minute here.

00:34:07.980 --> 00:34:10.760
Because you can't have your own child with Shelly, what do you do?

00:34:11.260 --> 00:34:15.430
You try to stake a claim on this one, Uncle Elvie, my eye.

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:20.440
Anybody who ever knew my uncle would think the same thing.

00:34:21.190 --> 00:34:25.340
Maurice, you're a lonely man with a lot of regrets,

00:34:25.720 --> 00:34:28.020
and you're trying to buy your way into a family.

00:34:29.270 --> 00:34:29.970
I don't blame you.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.560
Most people want a family.

00:34:34.030 --> 00:34:36.110
Look, why don't you come over

00:34:36.110 --> 00:34:37.810
and have a late supper with Walt and me?

00:34:37.950 --> 00:34:44.020
Come on.

00:35:03.196 --> 00:35:03.736
It's open.

00:35:04.988 --> 00:35:07.088
I'm Mrs. Capra. Hello, Dr. Capra.

00:35:07.168 --> 00:35:07.428
Yeah.

00:35:08.540 --> 00:35:09.680
Phil's remodeling the kitchen.

00:35:10.844 --> 00:35:11.344
Huh?

00:35:12.444 --> 00:35:12.944
Oh!

00:35:13.020 --> 00:35:13.520
Huh?

00:35:13.916 --> 00:35:14.476
How are your feet?

00:35:15.388 --> 00:35:19.108
kind of a pins and needles feeling, Ed, but I'm taking ibuprofen. Oh, good.

00:35:19.580 --> 00:35:20.680
I brought this for you.

00:35:22.620 --> 00:35:23.340
Don't tell me.

00:35:23.804 --> 00:35:24.804
Parkin' Boots.

00:35:25.532 --> 00:35:26.032
Huh?

00:35:27.484 --> 00:35:28.004
Nothing.

00:35:29.244 --> 00:35:29.744
Costumes.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:30.740
for the Founders Day parade.

00:35:31.690 --> 00:35:32.050
Costumes?

00:35:32.270 --> 00:35:32.590
Yep.

00:35:33.170 --> 00:35:35.350
Well, you know, I figured you and Dr. Capra

00:35:35.350 --> 00:35:36.290
had a pretty hard week.

00:35:36.390 --> 00:35:39.000
The woods, car, your feet.

00:35:39.400 --> 00:35:40.860
So I didn't think you'd have a chance

00:35:40.860 --> 00:35:41.600
to get anything together.

00:35:41.740 --> 00:35:43.740
I found this stuff in the basement of Ruthann's store.

00:35:45.250 --> 00:35:47.190
Well, that's really very kind of you, Ed,

00:35:47.250 --> 00:35:49.650
but I don't think we'll be going to Founders Day.

